{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5246",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with MS-1, as it is involved in multiple pathways that ultimately target MS-1. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704, which in turn is a target of palmarumycin CP18 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, both of which directly target MS-1. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Mollicellin N influences the activity of A704, which then modulates the activity of other compounds that ultimately affect MS-1. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Mollicellin N may interact with MS-1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on MS-1 suggests a possible regulatory or signaling role for Mollicellin N in the context of these pathways.",
